B.b_C=new A.aj("Salt the water like the sea","Use about 10 g of coarse salt per litre of water, and at least 1 litre per 100 g of pasta. The pasta seasons from within as it cooks \u2014 you cannot fully fix bland pasta with sauce afterwards.")
B.b_N=new A.aj("Always save the pasta water","The starchy, salted cooking water is the binder for nearly every sauce. Reserve a mugful before draining and add it a splash at a time while tossing to create a glossy emulsion that clings to the strands.")
B.b_M=new A.aj("Finish the pasta in the sauce","Drain the pasta 1\u20132 minutes before the packet time and let it finish in the pan with the sauce and a little pasta water. It absorbs flavour and the sauce tightens around it.")
B.b_F=new A.aj("Match the shape to the sauce","Long strands (spaghetti, linguine, bucatini) suit oil- and seafood-based sauces. Tubes and ridged shapes (rigatoni, penne, paccheri) hold chunky rag\xf9s. Small shapes (ditalini, tubetti) belong in soups. Egg pasta (tagliatelle, pappardelle) pairs with butter and meat rag\xf9.")
B.b09=new A.aj("The Roman quartet","Cacio e pepe (pecorino + pepper), gricia (adds guanciale), amatriciana (adds tomato), carbonara (gricia + egg). No cream in any of them \u2014 the silkiness comes from cheese, fat and pasta water.")
B.b0a=new A.aj("Real pesto is pounded, not heated","Basil, garlic, pine nuts, coarse salt, Parmigiano and Pecorino, and good olive oil, worked in a mortar or pulsed cold. Never cook pesto \u2014 toss it through hot pasta off the heat, loosened with pasta water.")
B.b08=new A.aj("Rag\xf9 is patient","A proper rag\xf9 bolognese is a gentle 2\u20133 hour simmer with milk added near the end. It should be rich and barely-there liquid, not a tomato soup with mince.")
B.b_R=new A.aj("Cook Mode & timers","Open any recipe and tap Cook Mode for a hands-free, step-by-step view with large type. Steps that mention a time show a tap-to-start timer; your place is kept if you leave and come back.")
